Article 2 (Submission of Business Plans)
(1) A business plan under Article 8 (1) of the Act on Facilitation of Cooperation in Local Agriculture and Fisheries Development Projects (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") shall include the following matters:
1. Name of the project;
2. Necessity for and purposes of implementing the project;
3. Target of the project;
4. Details, period, and implementation schedule of the project;
5. Methods and organizational structure for implementing the project (including matters concerning plans to entrust part of the project, where applicable);
6. Performance targets, performance evaluation indicators, and methods and timing of performance measurement for the project;
7. Project costs, detailed calculations of project costs, and financing plans;
8. The following matters concerning the person seeking designation as a private operating agency:
(a) Trade name, location, and contact information;
(b) Current financial position, organization, and personnel;
(c) Performance record concerning local agriculture and fisheries development projects and similar projects;
9. Other matters deemed necessary by the head of a local government.
(2) A private operating agency shall prepare an implementation plan containing the following matters and submit it to the head of the local government under Article 8 (6) of the Act. In such cases, relevant documents and drawings shall be attached where necessary:
1. Details of the project implementation plan under Article 7 of the Act;
2. The business plan under Article 8 (1) of the Act;
3. Details of the implementation agreement under Article 8 (5) of the Act.
(3) Where a private operating agency intends to request an extension of the period under the proviso of Article 8 (6) of the Act, it shall submit to the head of the relevant local government, before the deadline for requesting approval of the implementation plan, the reasons for the extension and the intended date of submission, in writing or by electronic mail or other means.
(4) Where the implementation plan submitted under paragraph (2) omits matters concerning the implementation agreement or fails to specify the details or methods of implementation sufficiently, the head of the local government may, under the proviso of Article 8 (7) of the Act, request the private operating agency to supplement the plan within a specified period.
